purpose: What does init detect and seed for a new project, and what does it deliberately not create?

Records that `engsys init --detect` fills only unset declarations and `--hooks` seeds a project-owned pre-push gate, with no document scaffold.
Translated from Korean to English; frontmatter, flags (`--detect`, `--hooks`, `--verify`, `--source`, `--generated`, `--lifecycle`), paths and the ADR 0006 link are unchanged.
Headings mapped to Decision, Background and Constraints, Rationale and Alternatives, Consequences, in source order; bold emphasis kept on the same phrases.
골격 rendered as scaffold and 배정 as assignment, per the glossary; "three packages" and the top-level-only detection limit are preserved.
No Korean literals retained; no facts updated to the current implementation.

